cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "fifth-power-concatenations: exhaustive GPU search for five-digit fifth-power concatenation identities"
abstract: >-
  CUDA implementation, mathematical coverage notes and recorded run evidence
  for an exhaustive search of ordered five-tuples (a, b, c, d, e) of
  five-digit integers (no leading zeros) satisfying
  a^5 + b^5 + c^5 + d^5 + e^5 = concatenation(a, b, c, d, e).
  The recorded run found exactly one solution,
  (74416, 50589, 59222, 49043, 82475).
authors:
  - given-names: Sai
    family-names: Bhushan
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/psimaths/fifth-power-concatenations"
license: 0BSD
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
keywords:
  - number theory
  - Diophantine equations
  - exhaustive search
  - meet-in-the-middle
  - CUDA
  - fifth powers
